From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:04:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grt: reroute only the resistance-aware nets in the final 3D
 pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the 2D route ends without overflow, FastRoute reroutes in 3D in
two passes, edges shorter than 40 gcells and then shorter than 12.
With resistance-aware routing on, both thresholds are lifted: both
passes rip up every edge of every net with negative slack, and the
second only widens the resistance-aware set (30 % of the critical nets
to all of them). On a block that routes without overflow that is most
of global route: 58.8 of 60.5 s of FastRoute on an asap7 queue of
61,321 nets. In the first pass 31,030 of the 37,198 nets ripped up are
not resistance-aware (a quarter of the 194 M gcells searched): they are
rerouted with the legacy cost on a route with no overflow to relieve.

The pass now runs once and on the nets resistance-aware routing
selected; without resistance-aware routing it is unchanged. On that
block: finalisation 62.1 -> 32.4 s, period at global route 992.1 ->
993.3 ps (+0.12 %); skipping the pass entirely would cost 1,004.2 ps.

TestResistanceMode checks that an unselected net routed on M3 keeps
its route through the pass, with a control that the same net is
rerouted onto M1 when resistance-aware routing is off. It moves the
goldens of res_aware_nets_percentage and resistance_aware_asap7_fr
(TNS -2619.2 -> -2626.5 ps, WNS unchanged, its PASS check holds); they
are regenerated if this goes upstream.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; retires with the //:bump onto
an OpenROAD that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
